      "text": "6,040.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **174** and **489**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can use the standard multiplication algorithm to calculate the product.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}174 \\\\\n\\times 489 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Digit\n1. **Multiply by 9 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 9 = 1,566\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 80 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 80 = 13,920\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 400 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   174 \\times 400 = 69,600\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}1,566 \\\\\n+13,920 \\\\\n+69,600 \\\\\n\\hline\n75,086 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{75,\\!086}\n\\]",
