      "text": "725 multiplied by 845 equals 610,375.\n</think>\n\nSure, let's solve the problem step by step.\n\n**Question:** What is the Product of 725 and 845?\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 725 and 845, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Write down the numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   725 \\times 845\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   We can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\,\\,\\,725 \\\\\n   \\times\\,845 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     \\,\\,\\,3625 \\quad \\text{(725 \u00d7 5)} \\\\\n    \\,\\,\\,50000 \\quad \\text{(725 \u00d7 40)} \\\\\n   + 580000 \\quad \\text{(725 \u00d7 800)} \\\\\n   \\hline\n    \\,\\,610375 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the partial products:**\n\n   \\[\n   3625 + 50000 + 580000 = 610375\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{610375}\n   \\]",
