      "text": "12,096.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **602** and **170**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can express **170** as the sum of **429** and **49**:\n\\[ 170 = 429 + 49 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 602 by 429\nFirst, calculate \\( 602 \\times 429 \\):\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n602 \\times 429 &= 602 \\times (400 + 29) \\\\\n&= 602 \\times 400 + 602 \\times 29 \\\\\n&= 240,800 + 17,458 \\\\\n&= 258,258\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 602 by 49\nNext, calculate \\( 602 \\times 49 \\):\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n602 \\times 49 &= 602 \\times (50 - 1) \\\\\n&= 602 \\times 50 - 602 \\times 1 \\\\\n&= 30,100 - 602 \\\\\n&= 29,498\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add the Results\nNow, add the two products together:\n\\[\n258,258 + 29,498 = 287,756\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{287,\\!756}\n\\]",
