  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "3,520,000.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **433** and **726**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can use the standard multiplication algorithm to calculate the product.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}433 \\\\\n\\times 726 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Digit\n1. **Multiply by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   433 \\times 6 = 2,598\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   433 \\times 20 = 8,660\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 700 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   433 \\times 700 = 303,100\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}2,598 \\\\\n\\phantom{0}8,660 \\\\\n+303,100 \\\\\n\\hline\n314,358 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{314,\\!358}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
