      "index": 0,
      "text": "73,148.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **560** and **500**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply the numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   560 \\times 500\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   560 \\times 500 = 560 \\times (5 \\times 100) = (560 \\times 5) \\times 100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate \\(560 \\times 5\\):**\n   \n   \\[\n   560 \\times 5 = 2800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply the result by 100:**\n   \n   \\[\n   2800 \\times 100 = 280,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{280,\\!000}\n   \\]",
