      "text": "52,958.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **712** and **182**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication to make it easier:\n\n\\[\n712 \\times 182 = 712 \\times (100 + 80 + 2)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 100:**\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 100 = 71,200\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 80:**\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 80 = 56,960\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 2:**\n   \\[\n   712 \\times 2 = 1,424\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results Together\n\\[\n71,200 + 56,960 + 1,424 = 129,584\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{129,\\!584}\n\\]",
