      "text": "295,861 multiplied by 95 equals 28,106,795.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **295,861** and **95**, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps using the distributive property. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n295,\\!861 \\times 95 &= 295,\\!861 \\times (90 + 5) \\\\\n&= 295,\\!861 \\times 90 + 295,\\!861 \\times 5 \\\\\n&= (295,\\!861 \\times 9 \\times 10) + (295,\\!861 \\times 5) \\\\\n&= (2,\\!662,\\!749 \\times 10) + 1,\\!479,\\!305 \\\\\n&= 26,\\!627,\\!490 + 1,\\!479,\\!305 \\\\\n&= 28,\\!106,\\!795 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{28,\\!106,\\!795}\n\\]",
