      "text": "214,523.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **916** and **971**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Write Down the Numbers\n```\n   916\n\u00d7 971\n```\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 916 by Each Digit of 971\n\n1. **Multiply by 1 (units place):**\n   ```\n     916\n   \u00d7   1\n   ----\n     916\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply by 70 (tens place):**\n   ```\n     916\n   \u00d7   70\n   ----\n   64,120\n   ```\n   (Note: 916 \u00d7 7 = 6,412; add a zero at the end to account for the tens place.)\n\n3. **Multiply by 900 (hundreds place):**\n   ```\n     916\n   \u00d7 900\n   ----\n   824,400\n   ```\n   (Note: 916 \u00d7 9 = 8,244; add two zeros at the end to account for the hundreds place.)\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\n```\n      916\n    +64,120\n    +824,400\n    ---------\n    890,436\n```\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{890436}\n\\]",
