  "model": "DeepSeekR1-Qwen-7B",
  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "399 \u00d7 981 + 639 \u00d7 88 = 897,482 + 1,602 = 900,084.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **217** and **729**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can break down the multiplication to make it easier:\n\n\\[\n217 \\times 729 = 217 \\times (700 + 29) = (217 \\times 700) + (217 \\times 29)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 217 by 700\n\\[\n217 \\times 700 = 217 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 1,519 \\times 100 = 151,900\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply 217 by 29\nFirst, break down 29 into 20 + 9:\n\n\\[\n217 \\times 29 = 217 \\times (20 + 9) = (217 \\times 20) + (217 \\times 9)\n\\]\n\n- **Multiply 217 by 20:**\n  \\[\n  217 \\times 20 = 4,340\n  \\]\n  \n- **Multiply 217 by 9:**\n  \\[\n  217 \\times 9 = 1,953\n  \\]\n  \n- **Add the two results together:**\n  \\[\n  4,340 + 1,953 = 6,293\n  \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add the Results from Step 2 and Step 3\n\\[\n151,900 + 6,293 = 158,193\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{158,\\!193}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
  "usage": {
