      "index": 0,
      "text": "110,096.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **206** and **428**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, let's break down the numbers into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n206 = 200 + 6\n\\]\n\\[\n428 = 400 + 28\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n(200 + 6) \\times (400 + 28) = 200 \\times 400 + 200 \\times 28 + 6 \\times 400 + 6 \\times 28\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **Multiply 200 by 400:**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 400 = 80,000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 200 by 28:**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 28 = 5,600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 6 by 400:**\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 400 = 2,400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 6 by 28:**\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 28 = 168\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n80,000 + 5,600 + 2,400 + 168 = 88,168\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{88,\\!168}\n\\]",
