      "index": 0,
      "text": "798 \u00d7 010 = 7,980.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **355** and **375**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, let's break down the numbers into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n355 = 300 + 50 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n(300 + 50 + 5) \\times (300 + 70 + 5)\n\\]\n\nThis results in the following multiplications:\n\n\\[\n300 \\times 300 = 90,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 70 = 21,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 5 = 1,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 300 = 15,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 70 = 3,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 5 = 250\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 300 = 1,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 70 = 350\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\times 5 = 25\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the multiplications:\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 + 3,\\!500 + 250 + 1,\\!500 + 350 + 25\n\\]\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n\\[\n90,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 = 111,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n111,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 = 112,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n112,\\!500 + 15,\\!000 = 127,\\!500\n\\]\n\\[\n127,\\!500 + 3,\\!500 = 131,\\!000\n\\]\n\\[\n131,\\!000 + 250 = 131,\\!250\n\\]\n\\[\n131,\\!250 + 1,\\!500 = 132,\\!750\n\\]\n\\[\n132,\\!750 + 350 = 133,\\!100\n\\]\n\\[\n133,\\!100 + 25 = 133,\\!125\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Final Answer\nAfter adding all the products, the final result is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{133,\\!125}\n\\]",
