      "text": "773,954 + 4,413 = 778,367.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **863** and **881**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   863 \\times 881 = 863 \\times (900 - 19)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 863 by 900:**\n\n   \\[\n   863 \\times 900 = 776,700\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 863 by 19:**\n\n   \\[\n   863 \\times 19 = 16,397\n   \\]\n\n4. **Subtract the second product from the first:**\n\n   \\[\n   776,700 - 16,397 = 760,303\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{760,\\!303}\n   \\]",
