      "index": 0,
      "text": "5,561.\n</think>\n\nTo find the **Product of 543 and 506**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication to make it easier:\n\n\\[\n543 \\times 506 = 543 \\times (500 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply by Each Part\n1. **Multiply by 500:**\n   \\[\n   543 \\times 500 = 543 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 2715 \\times 100 = 271,500\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 6:**\n   \\[\n   543 \\times 6 = 3,258\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results\nNow, add the two products together:\n\n\\[\n271,500 + 3,258 = 274,758\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{274,\\!758}\n\\]",
