      "text": "6,342.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **613** and **896**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nWe can use the standard multiplication algorithm to calculate the product.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}613 \\\\\n\\times 896 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Digit\n1. **Multiply by 6 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 6 = 3,678\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply by 90 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 90 = 55,170\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply by 800 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 800 = 490,400\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add the Results\nNow, add all the partial products together:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}3,678 \\\\\n+ \\phantom{0}55,170 \\\\\n+ 490,400 \\\\\n\\hline\n549,248 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{549,\\!248}\n\\]",
